the_finding:
Two same-language markets can NEVER both hold a row for one (family, entity, intent), because the generator collapses them before any row exists. In the main family loop:

    by_lang = {}
    for m in cand_markets:
        l = MKT_LANG[m]
        if l not in by_lang or demand_score(fid, m, tier) > demand_score(fid, by_lang[l], tier):
            by_lang[l] = m

One market per language wins each entity, on demand_score. So every same-language pair reads zero shared groups by CONSTRUCTION, and the four zeros reported for en-AU vs en-GB, en-AU vs en-US, en-GB vs en-US and es-ES vs es-MX are structural, NOT a result the cross-market gate produced. The gate's same-language rule is currently a no-op: it can never fire in this design. That is worth knowing because it was built to enforce exactly that rule.
